        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "E. Employees who are reinstated to employment after serving in military service shall receive their former job classification and rate of pay, plus any general increases applied to their former rate of pay since they entered military service. Step rate increases shall be applied only up to and including six (6) months continuous service on the rate of pay of full time and part time clerks, checkers, and wrappers who are reinstated to employment after serving in military service. Time spent in military service by apprentice meat cutters shall not be credited as time worked for purposes of accruing service on the progression scale.",
